> Elsa Gloria Synergy in an ALPHAstation 1200. =A0I was somewhat surprised
> when the resolution selected was 768x1024. =A0There doesn't seem to be a
> way to change it from the monitor menu (where it says the optimum
> resolution would be 1024x1280).
>
> Is there something I need to do from VMS to change the resolution? =A0Or
> on the graphics card itself? =A0Or at the console?
>
> Since I have much older machines and graphics cards with the high
> resolution, I assume this is possible.

From what I understand of these things..
Besides number of pixels (e.g. 1024 x 1280) pixel depth and refresh
frequency are also factors that play a role.
A monitor may be able to handle 1280 x 1024 at 72 Hz or 60 Hz but the
graphics card must be fast enough too.
Setting the refresh frequency to 72 Hz may reduce the maximum
resolution to 1024 x 768.
Pixel depth and resolution depend on available memory (on the graphics
card), the frequency depends on graphics processor speed.

Hans


