> Should I expect it to work on a 3-BNC-connector monitor, leaving the
> black and white cables disconnected?  (If so, and if it doesn't work,
> then I know the cable is bad.  If not, I don't know if the cable is bad
> but it is of no use for me now.)

If the DEC monitor has only 3 BNC connectors, then it is synch-on-green 
only, and most PC video cards don't deliver sync-on-green, but separate
horizontal and vertical sync signals (on the H and V cables).
So You have to study the video card owners manual to see if it can be put 
into sync on green mode.

