The cards one usually finds in DEC's workstations should
in principle work with DEC monitors of the same time frame,
so this may be one reason to keep an antique monitor.
I don't think the extra power consumption, compared
to a flat screen, is significant when compared to the
rest of your household's consumption.
Only a fraction of flat screens support SOG,
a list can be found here:
http://ps-2.kev009.com:8081/sog/

A problem with DEC monitors is, that they aren't
of good quality. Mine for example often refused
to work with ancient gfx cards, which gave a good
picture on other monitors.
It's also reported they frequently die when
switched on/off, so better leave them on.



