Please, name some part numbers (we're not all telepathetic).

DEC sold a variety of monitors (many of which were bought in and
available from other vendors with other badges).

Some of the workstation monitors, especially the later multi-sync
Trinitron ones, were really rather nice. I have only recently got rid
of one (but I already forgot its part number). Some of their
predecessors were fixed frequency sync on green jobs which are about
as much use today as a chocolate teapot. In between are things like
the VRC16 which is basically just a rebadged Taiwanese job; fine at
what it does, but at least for the VRC16 please do NOT assume that its
"power draw is probably negligible in comparison with everything
else".

DEC also sold a variety of graphics cards. Some of the older ones were
clearly DEC-specific and it shouldn't be too difficult to work out
what kind of monitor is required. The modern ones are mostly PC-
centric (VGA). In between are oddities like the TGA (ZLXp-etc) which
had VGA connectors but could do sync on green outputs.

VGA to 3BNC and VGA to 5BNC cables aren't DEC-specific and do appear
on eBay from time to time at reasonable prices, if that is what you
end up needing.

If you happen to have KVM switches in this picture, life gets more
complicated. For now, let's hope you haven't.


