>    dka400.4.0.9.0 has no media present or is disabled via the RUN/STOP switch
>
> on the console.

   I know nothing, but that looks like a generic read problem.
I'd guess that the "RUN/STOP switch" refers to a drive-disable
switch (as on an old MicroVAX), which you probably don't have
on this drive in this system.

> The media IS present and, as far as I can tell without having booted an
> OS, the CD drive is OK.

   I remember when "media" was the plural of "medium".  Those
were the good old days.

   The drive may be "good", but it may not be able to read
this disc.  Old optical drives tend to get dim and/or blind
over time, and CD-R[W] discs are less reflective than
factory-pressed CD-ROM discs.


